; Place an entity sprite (facing left or up) and test its hit box
;
; Entry point used by #R$B283 and #R$B436 (movers whose sprite faces left or up): D = x, E = y, H = y. Puts the
; position into the draw command and goes on to the hit box test with the first frame table.
;
; D X
; E Y
; H Y
@label=PlaceEntityLeft
c$B2C3 LD L,H        ; L = y
 $B2C4 LD H,D        ; H = x
 $B2C5 LD A,H        ; A = x in 2-pixel units
 $B2C6 EX AF,AF'     ; kept in A': its low two bits are the shift phase
 $B2C7 SRA H         ; x / 4: byte column
 $B2C9 SRA H         ;
 $B2CB LD ($ACD3),HL ; draw command position: (y, x/4)
; Entry point used by #R$B236: the position is already in the draw command. D = x, E = y, SP at slot+$C (the next words
; are the hit box). Tests the hit box against Jean and continues at #R$B2D4.
@label=TestEntityHitLeft
*$B2CE LD HL,$B2D4   ;
 $B2D1 JP $A851      ; #R$A851 tests the hit box, then jumps to the address in HL
